# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
# Leading slash: anchored to the repo root. An unanchored `build/` matches ANY
# directory named build at any depth, and silently excluded
# src/binomen/build/ -- the entire index-building subpackage -- from the first
# push. Nothing errored; the package simply was not there.
/build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Indexes and source archives are NOT committed ---
# They are large, and freezing a taxonomy in git reintroduces exactly the
# staleness this project exists to detect. Rebuild with `binomen-build-index`,
# or fetch a prebuilt release with `binomen-fetch-index`.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-journal
data/cache/

# NCBI archives, wherever they land. The repo root is where you actually end
# up downloading one, and it is 77 MB.
taxdump*.tar.gz
taxdump*.zip
*.dmp
!tests/fixtures/taxdump/*.dmp

# --- Build artifacts (release assets, not source) ---
/dist/
node/node_modules/

# --- Eval outputs ---
# The example run is committed so the report format is reviewable without an
# API key; real runs are not, and neither is anything with API responses in it.
eval/runs/*
!eval/runs/example-run.jsonl
!eval/runs/example-report.md
eval/verification-report.json

# --- Diagnostic captures ---
# Written by scripts/collect_boot_log.ps1. Copies of Claude Desktop's own logs,
# which are tens of MB and carry account ids, org ids, session ids and local
# paths. Useful while chasing a platform bug, never useful to anyone else, and
# not ours to publish. The scripts that produce them are committed; their output
# is not.
/diag/

# --- Working notes, not documentation ---
# Written for whoever is holding this project at the time, not for a reader of
# the repo. They go stale the moment they are true, name local paths and a
# local username, and answer questions nobody outside the working session
# asked. docs/TESTING.md is the public version of what INVOCATION-RUNS.md is
# the scratchpad for.
#
# HANDOFF.md and DISCOVERY-LOG.md were tracked until now; `git rm --cached`
# stops them growing, but they remain in history. That was judged acceptable:
# what leaked is a Windows username and two local paths.
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/DISCOVERY-LOG.md
docs/INVOCATION-RUNS.md

# --- Local editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Agent tooling, not part of the tool ---
# Skills, their lockfile and their per-repo configuration are how *this working
# copy* is driven; they are not functionality, documentation or tests of binomen,
# and packaging them would ship one person's editor setup to every user.
.claude/
.agents/
skills-lock.json
AGENTS.md
docs/agents/

# --- Session scratch ---
COMMIT_MSG.tmp
lpsn-icnp-100.json
# A personal working spec rather than project documentation. Delete this line if
# it should ship.
RUHEZC*.md
